# Decisive tune test. The integrator drives the true tilt down but too slowly, and the fins
# never saturate (peak 0.80) -- so authority is left unused. Crank P/I/D hard AND open the
# q-schedule (MOT_Q_REF 2500 -> 5000, so at boost q the fins are barely scaled down and get
# near-full authority). Two outcomes:
#   - true tilt driven < 8 in the high-q window, fins NOT hitting stops -> it's a TUNE, PASS.
#   - fins SATURATE (hit the stops) and it still holds > 8 -> genuine AUTHORITY wall, and the
#     fix is a bigger tab / less static margin (a design lever), now testable on a clean
#     estimate.
ATC_ANG_RLL_P 18.0
ATC_ANG_PIT_P 18.0
ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.8
ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.8
ATC_RAT_RLL_I 0.6
ATC_RAT_PIT_I 0.6
ATC_RAT_RLL_D 0.04
ATC_RAT_PIT_D 0.04
MOT_Q_REF 5000
